==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˌtæm.bɝ.ˈɹiːn/}}
* {{audio|en-us-tambourine.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{hyphenation|tam|bour|ine}}

===Etymology===
from {{etyl|fr|en}} {{term|tambourin|lang=fr}} (lit., "little drum"), from {{term|tambour||drum|lang=fr}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A [[percussion]] [[musical instrument|instrument]] consisting of a small, usually wooden, hoop closed on one side with a [[drum]] frame and featuring [[jingle|jingling]] metal disks on the tread; it is usually held in the hand and shaken [[rhythmic]]ally.

====Derived terms====
* [[tambourinist]]

